<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<workflow>
  <name>job_data_vault_create_link_run_tables_all</name>
  <name_sync_with_filename>Y</name_sync_with_filename>
  <description>Create all necessary link-run tables</description>
  <extended_description>This job loads creates a link-run table for every link in the Data Vault that has a status satellite and/or a validity satellite.

Normally the processing of a link consists of adding new entries and ignore already existing entries.
To be able to determine changes in a link with a business key (or deletes in case of a status satellite) all the records processed in the run must be available.
Because of this, a table is created for each link to contain all source records for the link in the actual run, both existing and new ones.
During the processing of the link this table gets loaded.

The process is:
1	Determine all the link-run tables to create
2	For each of those inputs:	a:	Create or replac the table with naming convention &lt;lnk_name>_run
						This table has exactly the same layout as the link table.
					b:	Create or replace the updateable view for this link-run table.</extended_description>
  <workflow_version>1.2</workflow_version>
  <workflow_status>0</workflow_status>
  <created_user/>
  <created_date>2014/12/15 01:09:50.587</created_date>
